The specification names three jobs for mitosis, and the paper asks for them by name:

• **growth** — you started as one cell;
• **replacing worn-out cells** — skin and gut lining are renewed all the time;
• **repairing damaged tissue** — a graze closes because cells divide.

Meiosis has one job only, in two organs only: making **gametes** in the ovaries and the testes.

• give the four numbers for mitosis — 1 division, 2 cells, the same chromosome number, genetically identical clones;
• give the four numbers for meiosis — 2 divisions, 4 cells, half the chromosome number, all genetically different;
• name the three jobs of mitosis and the one job of meiosis, and say where each happens;
• follow a chromosome number through meiosis, fertilisation and mitosis;
• choose the nuclei meiosis could produce, and name independent assortment as the source of variation.
